      "side": 1,
      "message": "I built and booted your 3-patch stack ([4365030](https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/kernel/common/+/4365030), [4365031](https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/kernel/common/+/4365031), and PS2 of [4347247](https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/kernel/common/+/4347247)) on a physical Pixel 6a (bluejay, 6.1.172-android14-11-g3fc92ed75e44) and ran both targeted micro-tests for each of the three patches and the full macro pressure benchmark suite from the bug.\n\nAll three patches work as intended and resolve the regressions cleanly:\n\n### Targeted Dragon Micro-Tests (85% RAM pressure with MGLRU 0x0003)\n\n- **Stale protection on targeted reclaim ([4365030](https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/kernel/common/+/4365030), upstream adb8213014b2)**: I set up a cgroup with a 48 MiB `memory.min` floor and 64 MiB of anonymous pages, triggered global reclaim so `kswapd` clamped it at ~48 MiB (caching `emin \u003d 48 MiB`), and then immediately wrote 16 MiB to its `memory.reclaim`.\n  - **Stock 6.1.172**: `memory.reclaim` failed with `-EAGAIN` (`rc\u003d1`, 0 MiB reclaimed, stayed at 47.9 MiB) because `get_nr_to_scan()` checked `mem_cgroup_below_min(memcg)` against the stale `emin` from global reclaim.\n  - **With your 3-patch stack**: `memory.reclaim` succeeded (`rc\u003d0`), reclaiming ~20 MiB down to 27.8 MiB on both top-level and nested `memory.min`-protected cgroups.\n- **Mid-scan `memory.min` boundary clamping ([4365031](https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/kernel/common/+/4365031), partial upstream 8aa420617918)**: When a cgroup starts at 64 MiB above its 48 MiB `memory.min` floor, global reclaim scans only the unprotected excess down to the 48 MiB floor (47.9 MiB retained) and rotates the cgroup to `MEMCG_LRU_YOUNG` once `get_nr_to_scan()` returns -1.\n- **Hierarchical protection calculation and `!lruvec_is_sizable()` ordering in `shrink_one()` ([4347247](https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/kernel/common/+/4347247) PS2)**:\n  - **Hierarchical `memory_recursiveprot`**: I tested a 2-level hierarchy (`system/dragon_hier` with parent `memory.min \u003d 96 MiB, memory.low \u003d 160 MiB` and two 64 MiB leaf children). On stock 6.1.172, because the intermediate parent cgroup is empty (`!lruvec_is_sizable()`), `shrink_one()` returned early before calling `mem_cgroup_calculate_protection()`, leaving parent `emin \u003d 0` and draining the subtree from 128 MiB down to \u003c1 MiB (0.7 MiB). With your stack, the subtree held 95.9 MiB (99.8% of its 96 MiB parent `memory.min` floor).\n  - **Zero false `memory.events.local:low` on empty intermediates or tiny cgroups**: Putting `if (!lruvec_is_sizable(lruvec, sc))` ahead of `mem_cgroup_below_low()` in `shrink_one()` (while keeping `mem_cgroup_below_min()` at the very top) completely prevented false `MEMCG_LOW` events. Across all ~250 cgroups on the device, zero empty intermediate cgroups (`/sys/fs/cgroup/system`, `/sys/fs/cgroup/apps`, `uid_*`, or `dragon_hier`) and zero non-sizable (`\u003c MIN_LRU_BATCH`) leaf cgroups emitted false `memory.events.local:low` increments (`delta \u003d 0`), while populated leaf cgroups genuinely reclaimed below `elow` incremented `memory.events.local:low` as expected.\n\n### Macro System Daemon Benchmark (Pixel 6a, 85% RAM / 4.75 GiB pressure hog, MGLRU 0x0003)\n\nWith `memory.min` floors configured on the 7 core Android system daemons (`/sys/fs/cgroup/system/uid_*/pid_*`, 2 tiers below root), stock MGLRU ignored the floors and evicted 60% to 99% of daemon RSS, whereas your 3-patch stack held every daemon right at its floor and cut system-wide swap-in churn by 68%:\n\n| Daemon | Stock 6.1.172 MGLRU (Pre -\u003e Post / Floor, File/Anon Refaults) | 3-Patch Stack `cur-inactive` (Pre -\u003e Post / Floor, File/Anon Refaults) | 3-Patch Stack `90% cur` (Pre -\u003e Post / Floor, File/Anon Refaults) |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| system_server | 502.0 -\u003e 319.8 / 412.6 MiB (1,334 / 13,814) | 570.7 -\u003e 432.7 / 446.2 MiB (63 / 0) | 562.7 -\u003e 422.0 / 429.2 MiB (1,938 / 1) |\n| SurfaceFlinger | 88.6 -\u003e 11.2 / 75.3 MiB (1,236 / 1,281) | 79.4 -\u003e 38.5 / 38.6 MiB (8 / 35) | 78.9 -\u003e 60.0 / 60.2 MiB (15 / 0) |\n| SystemUI | 65.7 -\u003e 1.2 / 54.4 MiB (76 / 6,395) | 68.0 -\u003e 58.6 / 58.8 MiB (0 / 37) | 67.1 -\u003e 47.6 / 47.8 MiB (166 / 910) |\n| composer | 7.8 -\u003e 0.3 / 6.7 MiB (56 / 187) | 8.3 -\u003e 5.4 / 5.6 MiB (1 / 0) | 9.3 -\u003e 6.4 / 6.5 MiB (0 / 0) |\n| audioserver | 11.7 -\u003e 0.2 / 9.8 MiB (1,297 / 661) | 10.7 -\u003e 4.4 / 4.5 MiB (29 / 0) | 11.6 -\u003e 8.8 / 8.9 MiB (0 / 0) |\n| cameraserver | 4.1 -\u003e 0.0 / 3.4 MiB (0 / 0) | 4.7 -\u003e 2.0 / 2.1 MiB (0 / 0) | 4.9 -\u003e 3.8 / 4.0 MiB (0 / 0) |\n| netd | 2.3 -\u003e 0.3 / 2.0 MiB (215 / 159) | 3.4 -\u003e 2.8 / 3.0 MiB (192 / 0) | 3.4 -\u003e 2.5 / 2.6 MiB (422 / 26) |\n| System `pswpin` | 76,490 pages | 24,568 pages (-68%) | 25,214 pages (-67%) |\n\nLGTM AFAICT",
